# .gitignore for a bare config repo (work-tree = $HOME)
#
# With `status.showUntrackedFiles no`, git already hides everything you haven't
# explicitly added — so this file is NOT about reducing status noise. Its job is
# to be a SAFETY NET: even if you fat-finger `config add ~/.ssh` or `add -A`,
# these patterns block secrets and junk from being committed. (You can still
# force one in with `config add -f` if you ever really mean to.)

# --- Secrets & credentials -------------------------------------------------
.ssh/
.gnupg/
.aws/credentials
.config/gh/hosts.yml
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
*.secret
.config/**/secrets*
.docker/config.json

# Machine-local shell overrides — keep these UNtracked on purpose so each
# machine has its own (see README "One repo, many machines").
.bashrc.local
.zshrc.local
.config/shell/local.sh

# --- History & caches ------------------------------------------------------
.bash_history
.zsh_history
.python_history
.lesshst
.wget-hsts
.cache/
.local/state/
*.swp
*~

# --- OS / editor cruft -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.Trash/
.viminfo
